# Styling and Primitive Rules

Use this rule when extracting styling, creating primitives, or cleaning repeated UI structure.

## Styling Goal

Keep the Lemon WMS UI consistent, matte, reusable, and predictable.

Do not restyle the app during structural refactors unless the task explicitly asks for a visual change.

## Styling Rules

- Preserve existing visual design during refactors.
- Extract repeated styling into primitives or reusable CSS classes.
- Keep one-off layout tweaks local.
- Avoid massive unreadable `className` strings when the pattern repeats.
- Use design tokens for repeated spacing, border, radius, typography, and muted text.
- Use `shadcn/ui` as the base component layer.
- Keep color accents intentional and data-driven.

## Design Token Areas

Prefer central styling for repeated design choices:

```txt
src/styles/tokens.css
src/styles/component-classes.css
```

Example token categories:

```css
:root {
  --dashboard-card-radius: 0.75rem;
  --dashboard-card-border: hsl(var(--border));
  --dashboard-section-gap: 1rem;
  --dashboard-muted-text: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
}
```

## Reusable Classes

Create reusable classes only for repeated patterns.

Good candidates:

- dashboard cards
- dashboard sections
- table shells
- modal shells
- form rows
- KPI card grids
- chart panels

Do not create a CSS class for a one-off style.

## Primitive Extraction Rule

Extract a primitive when a UI pattern appears in multiple places and has the same structural purpose.

Good primitive candidates:

- repeated KPI card layout
- repeated dashboard section wrapper
- repeated modal shell
- repeated details table
- repeated chart panel
- repeated empty/loading/error state
- repeated filter toolbar

Bad primitive candidates:

- one-off layout
- domain-specific business panel
- component that needs API knowledge
- component that hides mutations
- component that becomes a giant config object

## Skeleton Rules

Feature-specific skeletons:

- keep near the component they represent
- colocate when the skeleton only makes sense for that component

Generic skeletons:

- place in primitives
- use for project-wide reusable loading patterns

## Primitive Responsibility

A primitive may:

- compose `shadcn/ui`
- apply Lemon WMS styling
- provide reusable layout
- expose typed props
- render generic states

A primitive must not:

- fetch data
- mutate data
- import feature hooks
- know API response shapes
- know domain business rules
- hide feature-specific behavior
